{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1448322-how-big-can-cults-be","id":1448322,"title":"How big can cults be","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-12T08:04:38-07:00","id":1448322,"title":"How big can cults be","content":"I could not find a number to the size of a cult that a Mummy can have. Geist Krewes have a guide of 10 times Resistance trait, but I haven't seen anything for mummies. However, if I understand correctly, mummies can use Sybaris on onlookers and basically have all of them join the cult, so does that mean that a mummy can theoretically have dozens, if not hundreds, of followers in a very short time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T08:52:20-07:00","id":1448427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1448322-how-big-can-cults-be#post1448322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could not find a number to the size of a cult that a Mummy can have. Geist Krewes have a guide of 10 times Resistance trait, but I haven't seen anything for mummies. However, if I understand correctly, mummies can use Sybaris on onlookers and basically have all of them join the cult, so does that mean that a mummy can theoretically have dozens, if not hundreds, of followers in a very short time?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not as cut and dry as all of that. Sybaris causes an instinctive fear of death in mortals, which in part inspires them to comfort themselves in institutions that favor tradition, ritual and secrecy. Scorpion Cults are all of these things and therefore enjoy an uptick in recruitment when Sybaris is in the air. But the group Sybaris sufferers join might not be related to the mummy, or might be directly opposed to him. Sybaris might inspire people to get more intensely into local politics, join the freemasons, or form a hunter cell that specializes in killing things that rise from the grave. <br /> <br /> As far as I know, there are indeed no hard and fast rules about cult size. Very much up to the Storyteller. However, Cursed Necropolis DC does at least confirm that some mummy cults number in the 100s, although no cult is mentioned to reach the 1000s that I'm aware. It also states that with 17 mummies active in DC there are about 1000 cultists in total operating in the area for their various masters. That means about 50 cultists on average (ignoring for the moment that this average is completely arbitrary and a given mummy has fewer or more than this number) per mummy. Which makes sense if we assume those 50 are somewhat &quot;in the know&quot; and presumably have some influence over other ignorant people who go about doing their work and just happen to support the cult's agenda by proxy (assuming a high score in Reach and/or grasp). <br /> <br /> Mostly its up to the ST and the player. But the short answer is that yes there can be 100s in your cult depending on your needs and the backstory you've come up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}